  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3e4b5683c1ea36345958694d590b6436, type: 3}
  m_Name: Q4_Connectivity
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::QuizQuestionData
  questionText: A machine set to obtain an address automatically ends up with 169.254.14.7.
    What happened?
  choices:
  - It was assigned a public address
  - No DHCP server answered, so it gave itself an APIPA address
  - The subnet mask is wrong
  - It is connected to the internet through a router
  correctChoiceIndex: 1
  points: 10
  explanation: "169.254.x.x is what Windows assigns itself when DHCP fails. Seeing
    it points at the link or the DHCP server, not at the machine's own settings \u2014
    and it will not reach a 192.168.1.x host."
